Rather than this solution or that of disabling quitting altogether, both
of which have downsides - in particular this one does not permit us to
mock startscummers at all - why not simply run the logfile through a Perl
one-liner that strips all "quit with 0 points on turn 1" lines and counts
them up. This would take no time at all even for the current huge logfile;
the result could be passed to the real logfile analyser and made available
for downloading without eating such huge quantities of bandwidth. The
results from the oneliner could then form the "most shameless quitters"
results page.

Next year the "one minute between game starts" criterion seems an
excellent one.
